/* ---------- Card Battle world map ----------
   The owner asked for a world map like a classic fantasy adventure map: an illustrated continent with the Great Tree
   (55-clash-tower.js) in the middle and regions around it: a forest, a volcano, cursed woods, a magical forest, a
   desert and floating islands off the coast. Each region has its own tab (stages, lore and more later); for now every
   region tab only says "Coming soon", and the Great Tree opens the tree. The map art is one SVG (WM_SVG, generated
   once by a script: coast, region shapes with radial colour, scattered trees / dunes / mountains / dead trees /
   mushrooms / crystals, a river, a volcano, an oasis, pyramids, a moonwell, a haunted ruin, dotted trails, floating
   islands with waterfalls, ships, a compass rose and a parchment vignette); region shapes carry data-wr so a tap or a
   hover on them works like the labels. The labels (icon medallion, name, sub line and a bar: green when open) are HTML
   on top of the map, counter-scaled so they keep their size when zooming. The map pans by dragging and the edge
   arrows and zooms with the wheel and the + / − buttons; it always covers the view. Since the owner's second
   reference (an old printed province map) the whole map is one sepia ink on aged parchment: paper stains, coast
   ripple lines, a few ink symbols per region (trees, mountains, dunes, dead trees, star trees), rivers, a lake,
   dotted roads, dashed borders, the inked Great Tree, a compass rose with rhumb lines and a "The Known Lands"
   cartouche; regions all share the paper colour, and the labels are ink shields with sepia names. */

